@* D102, answered by the operator: the first download waits for somebody to accept the
   Minecraft EULA, since Mojang's own download page asks for it before its link works and
   the wrapper's download passes no such page. A page shows this only until the
   acceptance is recorded (BdsUpdateService.EulaAccepted). *@
<div class="eula-prompt">
    <p>
        Running a Bedrock server means accepting the
        <a href="https://www.minecraft.net/en-us/eula" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Minecraft EULA</a>.
        The wrapper downloads the server from Mojang once you have, and does not ask again.
    </p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" disabled="@Busy" @onclick="OnAccept">
        @(Busy ? "Downloading…" : "I accept and download")
    </button>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Records the acceptance and starts the download.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnAccept { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A download is under way.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Busy { get; set; }
}
